==Trivia==
[[File:PK01 Jynx edit.png|thumb|200px|Recolored Jynx in the ending credits]]
[[File:PK01 Jynx edit 2.png|thumb|200px|Another recolored Jynx in the ending credits]]
* For the Japanese Blu-ray release in 2012 of this [[Pikachu short]], {{p|Jynx}} was recolored in the ending credits due to the [[Jynx (Pokémon)#Controversy|controversy surrounding her color scheme]].
* This Pikachu short was adapted into the graphic novel [[All That Pikachu!]].
* All three {{OBP|Pokémon|species}} that debuted in this Pikachu short would later be made {{type|Fairy}}.
* This Pikachu short introduced [[Misty's Togepi]] as well as spoiled the Evolutions of [[Ash's Charizard]], [[Jessie's Arbok]], and [[James's Weezing]] to audiences in numerous countries, since it was released well before Togepi's [[EP050|hatching episode]] and the episodes in which the aforementioned Pokémon evolved ([[EP031]], [[EP043]], and [[EP046]]).
* This marks the animated series debuts of {{p|Pikachu}} and {{p|Meowth}}'s current, slimmer designs. These would become their species' default designs from [[Generation III]] onwards.
* At least one Pokémon of each [[List of Pokémon by evolutionary line|evolutionary line]] that evolved by [[Evolution stone]] at the time appears in this short.
* In the [[dub]], this is the only Pikachu Short where {{Ash}}'s [[Pokédex]], Dexter, provides narration. 
* Although genders were introduced in [[Generation II]], the ending credits shot at the ''onsen'' implies that [[Ash's Bulbasaur]], [[Brock's Geodude]], [[Ash's Pidgeotto]] and [[Jessie's Arbok]] are all male due to the presence of {{p|Jynx}} on the other side of the ''onsen’s'' divider, given that Jynx is a female-only species.
* [[Misty's Horsea|Horsea]] and [[Misty's Starmie|Starmie]] are Misty's only two reserved trained Pokémon at her Cerulean Gym not to appear in this short.

===Errors===
* When all of {{Ash}}, {{an|Misty}}, and {{an|Brock}}'s Pokémon stampede into the park, [[Misty's Psyduck]] is seen running over {{AP|Pikachu}}. However, in the next frame, Psyduck is seen standing right behind Pikachu.
* During the scene when {{p|Electrode}} rolls into frame right before exploding, an {{p|Eevee}} in the background has white eyes instead of black.
** In the same scene, a {{p|Primeape}}'s arms and legs are colored like {{p|Mankey}}'s.
* During the race between {{AP|Squirtle}} and {{p|Marill}}, several Pokémon appear in the background with incorrect sizes. These include {{p|Snorlax}}, {{p|Lapras}}, {{p|Cloyster}}, and {{p|Clefable}}, all of whom appear too small.
** Additionally, several coloring errors are present in this scene. {{p|Growlithe}} is shown with a miscolored muzzle, which is orange instead of beige, while Lapras's lower jaw is colored blue instead of cream.
* During the opening credits of the English [[dub]], [[Takeshi Shudō]] is mistakenly credited as the screenwriter of this short instead of [[Hideki Sonoda]].

===Dub edits===
* The Japanese writing of the [[Pokémon Theme Park]]’s name on the park’s entrance gate is replaced with the international [[Pokémon]] logo.
* Ash's [[Pokédex]], Dexter, acts as a narrator of sorts in the short, giving out various facts about the featured Pokémon and their behavior. These facts include:
** {{TP|Misty|Togepi}} is identified as the Egg Pokémon, although the species was later identified as the Spike Ball Pokémon. Togepi is also mentioned to have a low tolerance for hunger.
** {{AP|Bulbasaur}} performs a calming melody for Togepi, identified by Dexter as the "Bulbaby".
** {{p|Snubbull}} was identified as a "newly discovered" Pokémon.
** Pokémon are usually peaceful creatures who prefer to cooperate with each other, and will not usually battle unless instructed otherwise by their Trainers.
** The Pokédex is shown to be able to translate Pokémon languages.

